// TEST: Static Struct Array Field
// ============================================================================
// `static struct` asserts, once at the declaration, that every field type is a
// shape the static evaluator can carry as a value. An ARRAY field is not: the
// static world has no array StaticValue, so the assertion fails at
// REGISTRATION — before lowering — with the field named and the eligible
// shapes listed.
//
// Checking it at the declaration rather than at each use is the whole point of
// the marker: eligibility becomes DECLARED instead of re-inferred wherever the
// type is mentioned, so the error arrives once, at the place the author can
// actually fix, instead of arriving later at every use site.
//
// A plain `struct` with an array field is of course fine and untouched —
// corpus structs/011 is exactly that. Nothing about ordinary records changes;
// `static` only adds an obligation to the type that opted into it.
// ============================================================================
static struct Bad {
    a: Int,
    rows: Array<Float64 like Idx<3>>
}
// ERROR: BL3008
// ERROR-CONTAINS: array types are not statically evaluable
